package cajeta.net.http;

/**
 * Abuse-resistance limits for the incremental HTTP parser
 * ([`HttpParser`](HttpParser.cajeta), NET-7.3). A parser consults these
 * ceilings **while accumulating** the message head, so a hostile peer
 * cannot force unbounded buffering before the head terminator
 * (`CRLFCRLF`) arrives — the parser raises
 * [`HeadersTooLargeException`](HeadersTooLargeException.cajeta) the
 * instant a ceiling is crossed.
 *
 * ## The three ceilings
 *
 *   - **`maxHeadBytes`** — the total byte size of the head
 *     (request/status line + all header lines + the terminating blank
 *     line). The single dominant guard: it bounds the whole head buffer
 *     regardless of how the bytes are distributed across lines. Caps
 *     both the `header-flood` case (many small headers) and any single
 *     enormous line that on its own exceeds the head budget.
 *   - **`maxLineBytes`** — the longest a single CRLF-delimited line may
 *     grow. Catches a `long-request-line` / `long-header-line` flood
 *     early — before the whole-head ceiling — and gives a more precise
 *     diagnostic (which *line* blew the budget).
 *   - **`maxHeaderCount`** — the maximum number of header fields. Caps
 *     the `header-flood` case by count even if each line is tiny.
 *
 * The defaults mirror the common server posture (nginx
 * `large_client_header_buffers`, Go `http.DefaultMaxHeaderBytes`): a
 * generous-but-bounded head, ~8 KiB per line, ~100 fields. A caller
 * tunes them via the [`of`](#) factory for stricter or looser policies.
 *
 * This is a **pure value type** — no I/O — so it tests directly over
 * the JIT alongside the parser.
 */
public class HttpParserLimits {
    /** Total head byte budget (request/status line + headers + blank line). */
    public int32 maxHeadBytes;
    /** Longest single CRLF-delimited line (request/status or header line). */
    public int32 maxLineBytes;
    /** Maximum number of header fields. */
    public int32 maxHeaderCount;

    /**
     * Field-pinning constructor at the common-server defaults: a
     * 64 KiB head budget, an 8 KiB per-line cap, and a 100-field cap.
     */
    public HttpParserLimits() {
        this.maxHeadBytes = 65536;      // 64 KiB
        this.maxLineBytes = 8192;       // 8 KiB
        this.maxHeaderCount = 100;
    }

    /**
     * Explicit-ceiling factory. A non-positive value for any field is
     * normalized to that field's default (so a caller can override one
     * ceiling without restating the others by passing `0`).
     */
    public static #HttpParserLimits of(int32 maxHeadBytes,
                                       int32 maxLineBytes,
                                       int32 maxHeaderCount) {
        HttpParserLimits l = heap HttpParserLimits();
        if (maxHeadBytes > 0) { l.maxHeadBytes = maxHeadBytes; }
        if (maxLineBytes > 0) { l.maxLineBytes = maxLineBytes; }
        if (maxHeaderCount > 0) { l.maxHeaderCount = maxHeaderCount; }
        return #l;
    }
}
